maya: Quick flag 1: the OpenAPI examples for POST /v1/generate use `input` but our SDK snippets use `prompt`. Users copying examples get confused. Also the curl sample shows the response as an array but runtime returns an object.

nick: Which PR is this on?

maya: The docs PR I was reviewing: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/312. I left inline comments but wanted to coordinate before changing more.

sam: I looked — openapi components currently have:
```yaml
responses:
  200:
    content:
      application/json:
        schema:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/GenerateResponse'
```
But runtime returns an object: `{ id, choices: [...], meta }`. We should switch to `type: object` and set `properties.choices` to an array of choice objects. I'll prepare a patch for components/schemas/GenerateResponse.

jordan: Also the SSE streaming example in the API ref shows `event: token` frames; that's wrong. Our stream sends plain `data:` chunks (token pieces) and a final `data: [DONE]` (or `event: done` sometimes) — the doc should show raw `data:` handling. If people implement based on `event:` they break.

maya: Proposed plan: (a) standardize request param to `prompt` everywhere and add a short migration note; (b) fix response schema to object and update examples; (c) correct streaming example and add a Node snippet showing how to parse the raw stream.

nick: Ill own (a) + migration blurb. I can update OpenAPI examples and the Python/JS snippets in one PR so copy/paste matches. Will post link here.

sam: I'll do (b). I'll update components/schemas/GenerateResponse, adjust curl/python examples, and add a tiny test that validates example JSON against the schema to catch future regressions.

jordan: I'll take (c)  here's a minimal Node example to include in the ref:
```js
fetch('/v1/generate', { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify({ prompt: 'Say hi', stream: true }) })
  .then(res => {
    const reader = res.body.getReader();
    const decoder = new TextDecoder();
    let buf = '';
    const pump = () => reader.read().then(({done, value}) => {
      if (done) return;
      buf += decoder.decode(value, { stream: true });
      let lines = buf.split(/\r?\n\r?\n/); // SSE delim
      buf = lines.pop();
      lines.forEach(frame => {
        // frames are like: `data: {"delta":"Hi"}` or `data: [DONE]`
      });
      return pump();
    });
    pump();
  });
```
This avoids implying `event: token` which we don't emit.

maya: docs-bot flagged the branch in CI  openapi-lint/examples failing: missing required numeric example field `max_new_tokens`. I can add that to the examples in your PR, @nick, or you can add before merge.

docs-bot: CI | openapi-lint/examples failed  example request bodies must include required numeric fields. See https://ci.redwood-inference/internal/ci/12345 for logs.

nick: I'll add `max_new_tokens: 64` to the examples and push. I'll open a new PR that bundles (a)+(migration note)+examples sync.

sam: Regarding the Python SDK snippet: it currently shows `client.generate(input="...")`. I can change the code sample to `client.generate(prompt="...")`. Should we keep a note that `input` is an alias for now? Backend accepts both for a deprecation window.

maya: Yes, add one-line: "Deprecated alias `input`: accepted for now, please use `prompt`. Will be removed in next major." Keeps expectations clear.

jordan: After those patches land, I'll run a smoke pass on the internal examples site: SSE demo, curl output, and Python snippet. Ping me when merged.

nick: New PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/319  updates examples to `prompt`, adds migration note, includes `max_new_tokens` examples.

sam: I pushed schema changes into that PR and added tests/tests_examples.py which validates the example JSON objects against the OpenAPI schema during CI. That should catch array/object mismatches.

maya: Thanks — after merge I'll update the docs changelog and add a short entry to the SDK migration guide referencing the alias removal timeline.

jordan: Verified SSE example locally after the change  the Node snippet parses the stream fine. :thumbsup:

maya: Closing loop: once PR merged I'll deploy the docs preview and paste the preview URL here. Appreciate the quick turnaround!
